From: dagu
Subject: [PATCH] dagu: flush pending KMS update when the deadline timer is off

Against mutter 50.1 (Ubuntu libmutter-18 50.1-0ubuntu2.2).

update_ready() queues crtc_frame->pending_update when a page flip is
still in flight. schedule_process() only commits that queue if
is_using_deadline_timer() is TRUE. On dagu the KMS thread stays
NORMAL, so the timer is off and schedule_process() only
g_warning_once() — the atomic never goes out until something else
merges a later update. maybe_post is on time, dpu_enc_kickoff +100 ms
(B-kick).

Forcing the deadline timer on was worse (timerfd armed but dispatch
late). Flush the pending update on the deadline==FALSE path instead.

Live ELF:
  0x1bce48  cbz w0, warning  →  cbz w0, do_process_update

---
 src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
index 0000000..dagu0004 100644
--- a/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
+++ b/src/backends/native/meta-kms-impl-device.c
@@ -2257,14 +2257,22 @@ meta_kms_impl_device_schedule_process (MetaKmsImplDevice *impl_device,
                                                   META_KMS_UPDATE_FLAG_NONE);
         }
     }
 
   if (crtc_frame->pending_update)
     {
       MetaKmsImplDevicePrivate *priv =
         meta_kms_impl_device_get_instance_private (impl_device);
 
       g_warning_once ("crtc_frame->pending_update=%p, deadline_timer_state=%d",
                       crtc_frame->pending_update, priv->deadline_timer_state);
+      meta_kms_impl_device_do_process_update (impl_device, crtc_frame,
+                                              crtc_frame->crtc,
+                                              crtc_frame->pending_update,
+                                              META_KMS_UPDATE_FLAG_NONE);
     }
 
   if (!crtc_frame->submitted_update.kms_update)
     meta_kms_device_set_needs_flush (meta_kms_crtc_get_device (crtc), crtc);
 }
